 Mexican " [:a {:href "/athletes/901928"} "Ariadne Hernández"] ". Sauvage competed at the Paralympics between 1992-2004, winning nine gold and four silver medals. She would return in 2004 and place third in this event."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Tsuchida had a very interesting athletic career. She won medals at both the Summer and Winter Paralympics, in ice sledge racing at the Winter version, earning three golds, three silvers, and one bronze medal at the Paralympics overall. She also won the Boston Marathon five times consecutively, from 2007-11; won the Honolulu Marathon in 2003 and 2005, the Oita Marathon four times, in 1999, 2001, 2002 and 2003; and the 2010 London Marathon."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/901039"} "Louise Sauvage"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {} "1:56.07"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/901781"} "Wakako Tsuchida"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} "1:56.49"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/901928"} "Ariadne Hernández"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/MEX"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/MEX.png"}] "MEX"]] [:td {} "1:56.59"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/901551"} "Tanni Grey"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-a